@inherits OrbitComponentBase
@* "Set up this agent" (spec §6.14, §10.3), shown once after New agent or New token: the one-time configure command with Orbit's
   public address (App:BaseUrl) and the raw registration token, a Copy button, and how to run the agent. The token lives only in
   this page's memory: it is never stored, so leaving the page loses it (New token issues another). The Razor _AgentSetup partial. *@

<MudAlert Severity="Severity.Warning" Class="mb-3">
    <div class="mb-2">
        <b>Copy this command now. The token is shown only once, works once, and expires @Ui.When(Created.Agent.RegistrationExpiresAt).</b>
    </div>
    <div class="orbit-form-row">
        <MudPaper Outlined="true" Class="pa-2 orbit-key orbit-field-grow">@Command</MudPaper>
        <CopyButton Text="@Command" What="command" />
    </div>
</MudAlert>

<MudPaper Outlined="true" Class="orbit-card" Style="max-width: 60rem">
    <div class="orbit-card-header"><b>Set up "@Created.Agent.Name"</b></div>
    <div class="orbit-card-body orbit-small">
        <ol class="mt-0 mb-0 pl-4">
            <li class="mb-2">
                Put the Orbit Agent on a machine <strong>inside your network</strong> that can reach what it is for - the directory server, a Nagios instance.
                It needs outbound HTTPS to <code>@BaseUrlTrimmed</code> and nothing inbound - no firewall ports to open. (Publishing the agent is covered in
                <code>deploy/README.md</code>.)
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
                Run the <strong>configure</strong> command above in the agent's folder. It swaps the token for the agent's own credential and saves it next to
                the executable. That is the only setting the agent has: directory servers, Nagios instances and everything else are managed here in Orbit.
            </li>
            <li class="mb-2">
                Start it: <code>Orbit.Agent run</code> - or install it as a service so it survives reboots:
                <div class="mt-1">Windows: <code>sc.exe create OrbitAgent binPath= "C:\OrbitAgent\Orbit.Agent.exe run" start= auto</code> then <code>sc.exe start OrbitAgent</code></div>
                <div>Linux: copy <code>deploy/orbit-agent.service</code> to <code>/etc/systemd/system/</code>, then <code>systemctl enable --now orbit-agent</code></div>
            </li>
            <li>
                It shows as <MudChip T="string" Size="Size.Small" Color="Color.Success">Online</MudChip> under <a href="/Admin/Agents/Index">Agents</a> within a
                few seconds. Then set up the directory under <a href="/Admin/Directory/Index">Admin &gt; Directory</a>, or a Nagios instance under
                <a href="/Admin/Nagios/Index">Admin &gt; Nagios</a>.
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</MudPaper>

@code {
    /// <summary>The agent just created, or given a new token, with its raw one-time registration token.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public CreatedAgent Created { get; set; } = null!;
    /// <summary>App:BaseUrl, the public address the agent dials.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? BaseUrl { get; set; }

    private string BaseUrlTrimmed => (BaseUrl ?? string.Empty).Trim().TrimEnd('/');

    private string Command => $"Orbit.Agent configure --url {BaseUrlTrimmed} --token {Created.RawRegistrationToken}";
}
